WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.370
Athens, 399 BCE.

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.240
Outside a courthouse, two
men fall into conversation.

3
00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:11.190
One of them, Euthyphro, is
prosecuting his own father,

4
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.550
and he is sure the gods approve.

5
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.310
The other, Socrates, asks
him a simple question:

6
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.200
what is holiness?

7
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.290
Plato wrote their talk down.

8
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.280
Believers in one God still face
the puzzle it leaves behind.

9
00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.760
Is something good because God commands it,

10
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.670
or does God command it because it is good?

11
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.950
In this mission, you'll split that question
into two paths and follow where each

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.170
one leads.

13
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.770
Then you'll test the theory against
hard cases and weigh it up for yourself.

14
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:44.830
Your mission: find out what each
answer would mean for morality.
